"rationale":"No alternate generic name found. RAD001 is a development/research code and is already appropriately placed in pubmed_search_aliases.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19091655/"]},{"current_value":"RAD001","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"RAD001","rationale":"PubMed records identify RAD001 as everolimus, supporting use as a search alias.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19091655/"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA labeling confirms US-approved AFINITOR/AFINITOR DISPERZ everolimus products.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"TSC","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"TSC","rationale":"AFINITOR DISPERZ is FDA-indicated as adjunctive treatment for TSC-associated partial-onset seizures in patients aged 2 years and older.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Tablet; tablet for oral suspension","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Tablet; tablet for oral suspension","rationale":"FDA labeling lists AFINITOR tablets and AFINITOR DISPERZ tablets for oral suspension.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"5 mg/m2 once daily starting regimen; titrate to trough target","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"5 mg/m2 once daily starting regimen; titrate to trough target","rationale":"FDA dosing for TSC-associated partial-onset seizures starts AFINITOR DISPERZ at 5 mg/m2 once daily and titrates to trough 5-15 ng/mL.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Titrated to trough target; no single fixed max across patients","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"Titrated to trough target; no single fixed max across patients","rationale":"For TSC-associated seizures, FDA labeling uses BSA-based dosing and therapeutic drug monitoring rather than one fixed maximum daily dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Binds FKBP-12 to inhibit mTOR complex 1 (mTORC1), targeting dysregulated mTOR signaling in tuberous sclerosis complex.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"Binds FKBP-12 to inhibit mTOR complex 1 (mTORC1), targeting dysregulated mTOR signaling in tuberous sclerosis complex.","rationale":"FDA clinical pharmacology describes FKBP-12 binding, mTORC1 inhibition, and dysregulated mTOR signaling in TSC.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata AFINITOR/AFINITOR DISPERZ labeling","rationale":"The mechanism is supported by FDA labeling; replace DailyMed wording with an FDA/accessdata source for trusted-source concordance.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CYP3A4/P-gp substrate; not a clinically relevant inducer/inhibitor","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"CYP3A4/P-gp substrate; not a clinically relevant inducer/inhibitor","rationale":"FDA labeling identifies CYP3A4 metabolism and clinically important exposure changes with CYP3A4/P-gp inhibitors or inducers; it does not support clinically meaningful induction/inhibition by everolimus.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Inhibitor; Substrate / affected by modulators","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"Substrate / affected by modulators","rationale":"The row text and FDA label support substrate/affected-by-modulators classification. The \"Inhibitor\" filter is not supported as clinically meaningful.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"~30 h","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"~30 h","rationale":"FDA labeling states the mean elimination half-life is approximately 30 hours.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Liver and gut","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Liver and gut","rationale":"Supported as an inference from CYP3A4/P-gp disposition, hepatic impairment exposure increases, and predominant fecal recovery in FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established","rationale":"FDA labeling reports that single AFINITOR doses up to 50 mg did not prolong the QT/QTc interval in a placebo-controlled crossover study.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"GI/oral: stomatitis 64%, infectious: infection 50%, GI: diarrhea 24%, dermatologic: rash 21%, respiratory: cough 20%, constitutional: fatigue 14%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"GI/oral: stomatitis 64%; GI: diarrhea 22%, vomiting 10%; infectious: nasopharyngitis 16%, upper respiratory tract infection 15%; constitutional: pyrexia 14%; respiratory: cough 10%; dermatologic: rash 10%","rationale":"The current row mixes or misstates percentages for TSC-associated seizure use. FDA EXIST-3 high-trough AFINITOR DISPERZ data support stomatitis 64%, diarrhea 22%, vomiting 10%, nasopharyngitis 16%, upper respiratory tract infection 15%, pyrexia 14%, cough 10%, and rash 10%.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"2018 for TSC-associated seizures; 2009 original oncology approval","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"2018 for TSC-associated seizures; 2009 original oncology approval","rationale":"The AFINITOR label states initial US approval in 2009, and FDA orphan-drug records list marketing approval on 04/10/2018 for adjunctive treatment of TSC-associated partial-onset seizures.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=283609"]},{"current_value":"Epilepsy Society ASM list; Healthline ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata AFINITOR/AFINITOR DISPERZ labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; PubMed; ClinicalTrials.gov; EMA Votubia EPAR","rationale":"Healthline is outside the requested trusted domains, and DailyMed should not be used for boxed-warning verification. FDA, PubMed, ClinicalTrials.gov, and EMA sources support the retained facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01713946","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/votubia"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab; published=Mar 02, 2026; title=EVEROLIMUS TABLET [AUROBINDO PHARMA LIMITED]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab; effective_time=20260226; title=everolimus / EVEROLIMUS; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5","rationale":"DailyMed is not permissible for the FDA boxed-warning field; the FDA/openFDA API URL is the appropriate source.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5"]}],"generic_name":"everolimus","missing_rcts":[{"pmid":"39607729","proposed_link_text":"Kim2024|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39607729/","title":"Efficacy and safety of everolimus for patients with focal cortical dysplasia type 2.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39607729/","why_relevant":"PubMed/ClinicalTrials.gov identify this as a phase II randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled crossover everolimus trial in refractory seizures with focal cortical dysplasia type II (NCT03198949). Add if the CSV tracks all placebo-controlled seizure RCTs for the drug, with caveat that it is outside the FDA-approved TSC seizure indication."}],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"24.9 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: French2016 everolimus high-exposure trough 9-15 ng/mL 24.9%)","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"24.9 % (drug minus placebo RR50 differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: French2016 everolimus high-exposure trough 9-15 ng/mL 24.9%)","rationale":"FDA label Table 26 reports response rate 40.0% for high-trough everolimus and 15.1% for placebo; 40.0 - 15.1 = 24.9 percentage points.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/"]},{"current_value":"24.7 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: French2016 everolimus high-exposure trough 9-15 ng/mL 24.7%)","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"24.7 % (drug minus placebo MPC differential at maximum effective dose/regimen: French2016 everolimus high-exposure trough 9-15 ng/mL 24.7%)","rationale":"FDA label Table 26 reports median percentage seizure-frequency reduction 39.6% for high-trough everolimus and 14.9% for placebo; 39.6 - 14.9 = 24.7 percentage points.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/"]},{"current_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"NR/not extractable as a drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom patient-rate differential at the maximum effective dose/regimen from included phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT records","rationale":"The FDA label notes seizure-freedom rate as an additional outcome but does not provide an extractable drug-minus-placebo seizure-freedom differential in the cited table/abstract evidence used by the row.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/"]},{"current_value":"French2016|24.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/|366","field":"plot_diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"French2016|24.9|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/|366","rationale":"The plotted value and total randomized N=366 match EXIST-3 FDA label and PubMed citation.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/"]},{"current_value":"French2016|24.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/|366","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"French2016|24.7|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/|366","rationale":"The plotted value and total randomized N=366 match EXIST-3 FDA label and PubMed citation.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"GI/oral: stomatitis 64%, infectious: infection 50%, GI: diarrhea 24%, dermatologic: rash 21%, respiratory: cough 20%, constitutional: fatigue 14%","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"GI/oral: stomatitis 64%; GI: diarrhea 22%, vomiting 10%; infectious: nasopharyngitis 16%, upper respiratory tract infection 15%; constitutional: pyrexia 14%; respiratory: cough 10%; dermatologic: rash 10%","reason":"Corrects TSC-associated seizure EXIST-3 high-trough adverse-event percentages from FDA labeling.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Afinitor; Afinitor Disperz; Votubia","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Afinitor; Afinitor Disperz; Votubia; Zortress","reason":"Adds an FDA-recognized everolimus trade name relevant to the boxed-warning/transplant labeling; current listed names remain valid.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2018/021560s021lbl.pdf","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/votubia"]},{"current_value":"French2016|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"French2016|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/; Kim2024|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39607729/","reason":"French2016 is verified. Kim2024 appears to be an additional phase II randomized placebo-controlled everolimus seizure trial in FCD II, outside the FDA-approved TSC seizure indication.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39607729/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03198949"]},{"current_value":"PubMed loop 19/65 on 2026-05-15: 1 qualifying placebo-controlled randomized clinical trial report(s) retained from 9 PubMed candidate(s). Links were rebuilt from fetched PubMed PMID metadata and named FirstAuthorYear. Differential effectiveness columns summarize extractable maximum effective dose/regimen values within qualifying RCT reports.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"Audit 2026-05-20: French2016 (PMID 27613521) verified as phase 3 randomized double-blind placebo-controlled EXIST-3 everolimus/RAD001 adjunctive seizure trial in TSC-associated treatment-resistant focal-onset seizures. Kim2024 (PMID 39607729; NCT03198949) identified as an additional phase 2 randomized double-blind placebo-controlled crossover seizure trial in focal cortical dysplasia type II, outside the FDA-approved TSC seizure indication. Non-seizure TSC tumor/cognition/commentary reports should not be retained as ASM seizure-efficacy RCTs.","reason":"Updates RCT audit notes and rejects deterministic false positives such as TSC tumor/cognition/commentary papers.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01713946","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39607729/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03198949"]},{"current_value":"Epilepsy Society ASM list; Healthline ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata AFINITOR/AFINITOR DISPERZ labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; PubMed; ClinicalTrials.gov; EMA Votubia EPAR","reason":"Replaces non-trusted/unsupported source names with trusted domains used for this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01713946","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/votubia"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata AFINITOR/AFINITOR DISPERZ labeling","reason":"Mechanism is supported by FDA accessdata labeling; DailyMed wording should be removed from the cited source text.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab; published=Mar 02, 2026; title=EVEROLIMUS TABLET [AUROBINDO PHARMA LIMITED]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab; effective_time=20260226; title=everolimus / EVEROLIMUS; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5","reason":"DailyMed cannot be used for FDA boxed-warning verification; FDA/openFDA source is required.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"Inhibitor; Substrate / affected by modulators","field":"filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"Substrate / affected by modulators","reason":"FDA labeling supports CYP3A4/P-gp substrate/affected-by-modulators status, not clinically meaningful inhibitor status.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"French2016","pmid":"27613521","proposed_action":"Retain existing link.","rationale":"PMID 27613521 is the EXIST-3 report: adjunctive everolimus/RAD001 for treatment-resistant focal-onset seizures associated with TSC; phase 3, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled design; source links to ClinicalTrials.gov NCT01713946.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=boxed_warning_found; setid=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab; published=Mar 02, 2026; title=EVEROLIMUS TABLET [AUROBINDO PHARMA LIMITED]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=boxed_warning_found; spl_set_id=43ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab; effective_time=20260226; title=everolimus / EVEROLIMUS; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5","reason":"Black-box warning field must use FDA/openFDA, FDA label, or Drugs@FDA, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata AFINITOR/AFINITOR DISPERZ labeling","reason":"Mechanism source should cite FDA accessdata label rather than DailyMed wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Epilepsy Society ASM list; Healthline ASM list; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/accessdata AFINITOR/AFINITOR DISPERZ labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling; PubMed; ClinicalTrials.gov; EMA Votubia EPAR","reason":"Current evidence_sources includes non-trusted or non-preferred sources for this audit; replacement sources support the row facts.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2022/203985s023%2C022334s051lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2243ef3c29-0e25-4fdd-aea1-06a20af9bbab%22&limit=5","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27613521/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01713946","https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/human/EPAR/votubia"]}],"summary":"Everolimus row is mostly supportable, but needs updates: replace DailyMed black-box source with FDA/openFDA, correct TSC-seizure adverse-event percentages, remove unsupported enzyme \"Inhibitor\" filter, replace weak evidence_sources, add Zortress as a trade name, and consider adding Kim2024/PMID 39607729 as an additional placebo-controlled phase II seizure RCT outside the FDA-approved TSC indication. French2016/PMID 27613521 and the RR50/MPC differentials are verified."}
